# The self-improvement loop of d40, d42 and d44: a correction is filed as a lesson by
# whoever made it, the improver reads lessons rather than free text, and every lesson
# leaves the pile by a commit or by an answered rejection, never by deletion.
$ maestro lesson file "the Lead dispatched a lane for a one-line doc fix" --expected "a one-line diff is done in place, with a card only for the claim" --why "a contract longer than the diff costs more than it protects" --target "recipe slp, Lane procedure" --evidence w41 --evidence h7
l1 [pending] the Lead dispatched a lane for a one-line doc fix
target: recipe slp, Lane procedure
expected: a one-line diff is done in place, with a card only for the claim
why: a contract longer than the diff costs more than it protects
evidence: w41, h7
project: repo

$ maestro lesson file "the report named a candidate that was never verified" --expected "a done report names the sha the falsifier actually ran against" --why "an unverified candidate makes the gate a formality" --target "lead.md, reporting rule" --evidence w44
l2 [pending] the report named a candidate that was never verified
target: lead.md, reporting rule
expected: a done report names the sha the falsifier actually ran against
why: an unverified candidate makes the gate a formality
evidence: w44
project: repo

$ maestro lesson list
l1 [pending] (repo) recipe slp, Lane procedure | the Lead dispatched a lane for a one-line doc fix
l2 [pending] (repo) lead.md, reporting rule | the report named a candidate that was never verified

$ maestro lesson show l1
